# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers, where a CRLF line ending makes
# `#!/bin/sh` name an interpreter called "sh" plus a carriage return, which
# doesn't exist — the container exits the moment it starts. Git on Windows
# (core.autocrlf) would otherwise check them out with CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Quantized-mesh terrain tiles are binary. Git usually detects that, but
# this repo is used with core.autocrlf on Windows, and a tile misread as text
# would have its bytes "fixed" on checkout — a corrupt tile doesn't error in
# the browser, it silently stops the terrain refining. Say so explicitly.
*.terrain binary
